Overall Summary of AWS IAM and S3 Practical Examination (Tasks 1–11)

**Introduction**:-
The AWS IAM and S3 practical examination helped me understand the fundamental concepts of cloud security, identity management, access control, and storage management 
using Amazon Web Services (AWS). In this practical, I learned how to create IAM users and groups, attach AWS-managed policies, create custom policies, configure IAM roles for EC2, 
and verify permissions. I also learned how to create and secure S3 buckets, organize objects, enable versioning, configure bucket policies, create lifecycle rules, 
enable server access logging, and understand encryption and access controls This practical gave me hands-on experience with the AWS Management Console and 
helped me understand how to manage cloud resources securely and efficiently.

 **What I Learned from This Practical**:-
1. Creating and managing IAM users and groups.
2. Applying AWS-managed and customer-managed policies.
3. Following the principle of least privilege.
4. Creating IAM roles and using temporary credentials for AWS services.
5. Testing and verifying access permissions.
6. Creating secure S3 buckets and uploading objects.
7. Organizing objects and managing their versions.
8. Configuring bucket policies and resource ARNs.
9. Automating storage management through lifecycle rules.
10. Configuring and verifying server access logging.
11. Understanding encryption and preventing accidental public access.
I also learned the importance of taking screenshots of the actual configurations and test results as evidence of successful practical work

**Final Conclusion**
In conclusion, the AWS IAM and S3 practical examination helped me develop a better understanding of cloud computing, 
identity and access management, data storage, and security Through the eleven tasks, I learned how to create and manage users, groups, policies, and roles; configure permissions;
secure S3 buckets; organize object; enable versioning; create lifecycle rules; and configure server access logging.
Although I faced challenges with policy configuration, permission errors, version management, and delayed log delivery, 
these challenges helped me understand the importance of troubleshooting, validating configurations, and following AWS security best practices.
This practical strengthened my confidence in using the AWS Management Console and taught me the importance of the principle of least privilege, 
encryption access control, and data protection. The knowledge gained from these tasks will help me perform future AWS administration activities more confidently and securely.
